---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
const lastUpdated = "27 April 2026";
---
<Layout
  title="Terms of Service | Interlock Alert"
  description="The terms governing access to and use of Interlock Alert's website, alcohol interlock devices, customer portal and related services."
>
  <section class="hero hero--inner">
    <div class="hero__bg" aria-hidden="true"></div>
    <div class="wrap hero__grid hero__grid--narrow">
      <div class="hero__copy reveal">
        <span class="eyebrow">Legal</span>
        <h1 class="display">Terms of Service</h1>
        <p class="hero__sub">Last updated: {lastUpdated}.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--band">
    <div class="wrap wrap--narrow">
      <article class="legal reveal">
        <h2>1. About these terms</h2>
        <p>These Terms of Service ("Terms") govern your access to and use of the Interlock Alert website, alcohol interlock devices, customer portal and related services ("Services") supplied by Interlock Alert Ltd ("Interlock Alert", "we", "our", "us"), registered at Village Hall, Clifton, Penrith, CA10 2EA. By using the Services you agree to these Terms. If you are entering into these Terms on behalf of an organisation, you confirm that you have authority to bind that organisation.</p>

        <h2>2. Definitions</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Customer</strong> — the person or organisation that has entered into a service agreement with Interlock Alert.</li>
          <li><strong>Device</strong> — an Interlock Alert alcohol interlock unit fitted to a vehicle under a service agreement.</li>
          <li><strong>Portal</strong> — the customer-facing web application used to administer Devices, drivers and reports.</li>
          <li><strong>Driver</strong> — any individual who provides a breath sample on a Device fitted to a Customer's vehicle.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>3. Service agreement</h2>
        <p>Provision of Devices and the Portal is governed by a separate written service agreement entered into between Interlock Alert and the Customer. The service agreement covers commercial terms, term length, installation arrangements, support, service levels, fees, and Customer-specific data handling rules. These Terms apply where they do not conflict with the service agreement; in the event of conflict, the service agreement prevails.</p>

        <h2>4. Use of the website and Portal</h2>
        <p>You may use the website and Portal only for their intended purpose. You agree not to:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Reverse engineer, decompile or attempt to extract source code from any part of the Services.</li>
          <li>Interfere with the security or integrity of the Services, or attempt unauthorised access to systems, accounts or data.</li>
          <li>Use the Services to transmit unlawful, infringing, or harmful content.</li>
          <li>Resell or sub-licence access to the Portal without our prior written consent.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>5. Devices and installation</h2>
        <p>Devices remain the property of Interlock Alert (or the financing party named in the service agreement). Installation is carried out by certified engineers and integrates with the vehicle's ignition system. The Customer is responsible for ensuring that the vehicle is in a roadworthy state at the time of installation, that the work is authorised by the vehicle's owner or registered keeper, and that any third-party warranty or insurance terms are not breached by fitting the Device.</p>
        <p>Tampering with, modifying or attempting to disable a Device — or instructing or permitting any person to do so — constitutes a material breach of these Terms.</p>

        <h2>6. Drivers and identification</h2>
        <p>Each test event recorded by a Device is captured with a still image and (where configured) a short video clip of the person providing the breath sample. The Customer is responsible for ensuring that all Drivers have been informed of this, and where required has been provided with appropriate notices, training and consent under the Customer's own data protection arrangements.</p>

        <h2>7. Fees and payment</h2>
        <p>Fees are set out in the service agreement. Unless agreed otherwise in writing, fees are billed monthly in advance, payable within 14 days of invoice date. Late payment may attract interest in line with the Late Payment of Commercial Debts (Interest) Act 1998. Pilot programmes are governed by separate pilot terms agreed in advance.</p>

        <h2>8. Service availability</h2>
        <p>We use reasonable endeavours to keep the Portal available 24 hours a day. Planned maintenance is communicated in advance where possible. Devices continue to function for breath testing during a portal or 4G outage; queued test events sync to the Portal once connectivity is restored.</p>

        <h2>9. Intellectual property</h2>
        <p>All intellectual property rights in the Services — including the website, Portal, Devices and supporting documentation — are owned by Interlock Alert or its licensors. The Customer is granted a non-exclusive, non-transferable, non-sublicensable licence to use the Services solely as contemplated by the service agreement and these Terms.</p>

        <h2>10. Customer data</h2>
        <p>Personal data processed through the Services is handled in accordance with our <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>. Where Interlock Alert processes data on the Customer's behalf, the data processing addendum to the service agreement governs that processing.</p>

        <h2>11. Liability</h2>
        <p>Nothing in these Terms limits any liability that cannot legally be limited, including liability for death or personal injury caused by negligence and liability for fraud. Subject to that, our total liability arising under or in connection with the Services is limited to the fees paid by the Customer in the twelve months preceding the event giving rise to liability. We are not liable for any indirect or consequential loss, loss of profits, loss of business or loss of goodwill.</p>
        <p>Interlock Alert provides risk-control technology. The decision to permit any individual to drive remains the responsibility of the Customer (where the vehicle is operated by a fleet or business) or of the individual driver. A pass result on a Device does not warrant fitness to drive in any other respect.</p>

        <h2>12. Termination</h2>
        <p>Either party may terminate the service agreement in line with the termination clauses set out in that agreement. On termination, the Customer will return any Interlock Alert-owned hardware, and we will arrange removal of Devices from vehicles where required. Removal returns the vehicle to its original wiring state.</p>

        <h2>13. Governing law and jurisdiction</h2>
        <p>These Terms and any dispute or claim arising out of or in connection with them are governed by the laws of England and Wales. The courts of England and Wales have exclusive jurisdiction.</p>

        <h2>14. Changes to these Terms</h2>
        <p>We may update these Terms from time to time. The "last updated" date at the top of this page shows when the most recent change was made. Material changes affecting active customers will be communicated in advance.</p>

        <h2>15. Contact</h2>
        <p>Email <a href="mailto:hello@interlockalert.co.uk">hello@interlockalert.co.uk</a> or write to: Interlock Alert Ltd, Village Hall, Clifton, Penrith, CA10 2EA.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
